    "objectID": "index.html",
    "href": "index.html",
    "title": "Causal Inference in Clinical Medical Research",
    "section": "",
    "text": "Preface\nCausal inference is a central scientific approach to studying cause-and-effect relationships: its core aim is to determine whether a cause produces an effect and how large that effect is. This book systematically introduces causal-inference methods for contemporary clinical medical research, spanning randomized controlled trials; real-world study designs based on propensity scores, instrumental variables, regression discontinuity, and time-series analysis; and machine-learning- and AI-driven causal inference.\nThe book is intended as an advanced text in medical statistics for medical students, clinical researchers, and researchers in statistics and artificial intelligence.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNoteAbout this online edition\n\n\n\nThis book is available in 中文 and English, released free online. Companion datasets are in the repository data/ directory; code examples accompany each chapter.\n\n\n\nHow to cite: Qiao N. Causal Inference in Clinical Medical Research. Online edition, 2026. (DOI to be added)",
    "crumbs": [
      "Preface"
    ]
  },
